# Arrays + Loops Together

This is MASSIVE.

You practiced:

```ruby id="6tdxlu"
while x < numbers.length
```

This teaches:

* dynamic looping
* scalability

Why `.length` matters:

Bad:

```ruby id="yw0xy5"
while x < 2
```

Good:

```ruby id="5h53um"
while x < numbers.length
```

Because now the code works no matter how many items exist.

That’s real engineering thinking.

---

# Real Backend Example

Imagine your Rails app:

```ruby id="c8oyr8"
